      "writtenOn": "2025-07-02T02:48:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that we need to get confirmation from Albert Wang(\nalbertccwang@google.com) and Puma Hsu about this change. Using \u0027Restricted vh\u0027 from android14-5.15 is on purpose, I think. Becasue, Googling says that restricted vh is desgigned to work under specific condition such as AP is offline. So, our usb_dev_SUSPEND() vendor hook must be defined as \u0027Restricted\u0027 vh to be executed during suspend process. Let\u0027e ask why to Alber Wang who made the rvh change patch on android14-5.15 or Puma Hsu who is the author of these patch sets.\n(* I\u0027ve already tested the usb-audio low power call scenario with rh__usb_dev_suspend(). It works on normal situation well but could be malfuntion under abnormal or corner case, I think) \n\n\nGoogling-Gemini: \u0027Vendor hooks are a more general mechanism for adding custom functionality, while restricted vendor hooks are specifically designed for situations where a hook must be executed under specific conditions, even if the CPU is offline or in a non-atomic context.\u0027",
      "parentUuid": "5657f6b7_9deb2602",
